2 345/161 kV double circuit (MISO-SPP JTIQ)</name><styleUrl>#planned</styleUrl><ExtendedData><Data name="feature_type"><value>line</value></Data><Data name="id"><value>misor-jtiq-raun-s3452-345</value></Data><Data name="name"><value>Raun - S3452 345/161 kV double circuit (MISO-SPP JTIQ)</value></Data><Data name="kv"><value>345</value></Data><Data name="project_type"><value>new line</value></Data><Data name="miles_new"><value>0</value></Data><Data name="miles_upgraded"><value>0</value></Data><Data name="purpose"><value>shared grid</value></Data><Data name="tappable"><value>yes</value></Data><Data name="tap_note"><value>The line itself can be tapped (345 kV and below)</value></Data><Data name="from"><value>Raun Substation (MidAmerican)</value></Data><Data name="to"><value>S3452 345 kV Substation (new, expansion of OPPD S1252 north of Omaha)</value></Data><Data name="county_from"><value>Woodbury</value></Data><Data name="recommended_next_step"><value>substation campaign</value></Data><Data name="recommendation_reason"><value>End substations are known; the route is not final yet.</value></Data><Data name="priority_score"><value>45.0</value></Data><Data name="program"><value>MISO (utility and state filings)</value></Data><Data name="route_status"><value>end substations only</value></Data><Data name="first_seen"><value>2026-11-13</value></Data><Data name="market"><value>MISO</value></Data><Data name="state"><value>IA, NE</value></Data><Data name="source"><value>https://spp.org/documents/73601/oppd%20jtiq%20ntc%20220873.pdf; https://www.spp.org/documents/72223/20240816_revisions%20to%20spp-miso%20joa%20to%20implement%20jtiq_er24-2798-000.pdf; https://cdn.misoenergy.org/20241212%20Board%20of%20Directors%20Item%2009a%20MTEP%20Executive%20Summary%20Appdendix%20A%20Appendix%20F665158.pdf</value></Data><Data name="stage"><value>planned</value></Data><Data name="stage_detail"><value>JTIQ project approved by MISO (MTEP24) and SPP boards Dec 2024: new 345/161 kV double circuit from Raun replacing Raun-Tekamah-S1226 161 kV; the MISO/MTEP24 table gives in service 2031 (MEC-OPPD). SPP NTC 220873 covers about 72 mi of 345 kV from S3452 to the OPPD/MEC demarcation; the length of MidAmerican's Iowa part is not stated. Raun county is not stated in sources (Raun is near Sioux City); no Iowa franchise docket found.</value></Data><Data name="builder"><value>MidAmerican Energy (Iowa end) / Omaha Public Power District (Nebraska, SPP)</value></Data><Data name="from_status"><value>existing, expanding</value></Data><Data name="from_there_now"><value>yes</value></Data><Data name="from_work"><value>adding to it (new line, transformer or expansion)</value></Data><Data name="from_work_stage"><value>planned</value></Data><Data name="to_status"><value>existing, expanding</value></Data><Data name="to_there_now"><value>yes</value></Data><Data name="to_work"><value>adding to it (new line, transformer or expansion)</value></Data><Data name="to_work_stage"><value>planned</value></Data><Data name="location_quality"><value>unknown</value></Data><Data name="queue_projects"><value>0</value></Data><Data name="queue_mw"><value>0</value></Data><Data name="geometry_note"><value>Only one end substation can be placed; point at that end</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>-96.36546,42.32936,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Carson - Midlothian 500 kV Line #563 rebuild</name><styleUrl>#planned</styleUrl><ExtendedData><Data name="feature_type"><value>line</value></Data><Data name="id"><value>pjmr-dom-carson-midlothian-500-rebuild</value></Data><Data name="name"><value>Carson - Midlothian 500 kV Line #563 rebuild</value></Data><Data name="kv"><value>500</value></Data><Data name="project_type"><value>upgrade</value></Data><Data name="miles_new"><value>0</value></Data><Data name="miles_upgraded"><value>37.4</value></Data><Data name="purpose"><value>shared grid</value></Data><Data name="tappable"><value>maybe</value></Data><Data name="tap_note"><value>M